From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: jrash <johnrash@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 15:54:03 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 115/342] disk device manager: don't unregister a file device
 that is mounted

DeleteFileDevice() removed a disk image's device even with a volume
mounted from it, which then lost its device under it ("diskimage
unregister" on a mounted image ended in a panic). It now fails with
B_BUSY while the device or any of its partitions is mounted.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/system/kernel/disk_device_manager/KDiskDeviceManager.cpp | 3 +++
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/system/kernel/disk_device_manager/KDiskDeviceManager.cpp b/src/system/kernel/disk_device_manager/KDiskDeviceManager.cpp
index bd6813f5db..b5e197da54 100644
--- a/src/system/kernel/disk_device_manager/KDiskDeviceManager.cpp
+++ b/src/system/kernel/disk_device_manager/KDiskDeviceManager.cpp
@@ -828,6 +828,9 @@ KDiskDeviceManager::DeleteFileDevice(partition_id id)
 		if (!dynamic_cast<KFileDiskDevice*>(device) || id != device->ID())
 			return B_ENTRY_NOT_FOUND;
 		if (DeviceWriteLocker locker = device) {
+			// a mounted file system would lose its device under it
+			if (device->IsMounted() || device->IsChildMounted())
+				return B_BUSY;
 			if (_RemoveDevice(device))
 				return B_OK;
 		}
